+### ⚠️ Sensitive capability disclosure (M12)
+
+J.A.R.V.I.S. legitimately asks for the same combination of capabilities that
+stalkerware uses: **Accessibility Service** (reads the screen, performs taps),
+**Notification Listener** (reads email/SMS bodies), **Device Administrator**
+(lock screen / wipe), plus SMS, call log, contacts and location.
+
+That combination is exactly why Google Play Protect warns about apps like this,
+and why the permission list was pruned (see `patches/security/NOTES.md`, C6).
+Concretely, in this build:
+
+- Every one of the remaining permissions has a call site in `lib/` or
+  `android/app/src/main/kotlin/`; anything without one was removed.
+- `MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` stays because the file tool writes to real
+  Downloads/Documents paths. It is a Play-policy-restricted permission, so this
+  app is a **personal sideload**, not a Play Store submission.
+- Nothing is granted silently: each special access is requested from the
+  Permissions Hub and can be revoked at any time in Android Settings.
+- Accessibility node dumps and notification bodies are held in memory only for
+  the duration of a task; notification bodies are additionally purged on screen
+  off and capped (M6).
+- SMS and outbound calls are behind an explicit native confirmation gate (H5),
+  so the LLM cannot dial or text without a human approving it.
+
+If you install this on someone else's device, that is spyware. Don't.
+
